Stop and save
= 

Start now
= 

Start a chart from here, for one that's already under way. Set the slant by hand if it leans.
= 

Centre %.0f Hz
= 

Where the signal's centre is heard: the midpoint of its black at -400 Hz and its white at +400 Hz
= 

Slant %+.0f ppm
= 

Trims the line length, to straighten a chart that leans. A chart that starts with phasing measures this for itself.
= 

No chart yet. In USB, set the dial 1.9 kHz below the station's listed frequency. A chart starts by itself when its start tone or phasing is heard.
