YOU
= 

Your locator
= 

Your Maidenhead locator, such as IO91WM. It goes in exported logs, and the Log tab uses it to give a distance.
= 

QRZ.com username
= 

For finding stations on the map that aren't in your log. Needs a QRZ.com XML subscription to give their locator or position.
= 

QRZ.com password
= 

Kept in settings.ini in the data folder, as plain text.
= 

HamQTH username
= 

For finding stations on the map, free: make an account at hamqth.com. Asked after QRZ.com, or alone if there's no QRZ.com login.
= 

HamQTH password
= 

Log date format
= 

How dates are shown in the log, in UTC. The Log tab leaves out the year to save room. Exported logs, and the log file itself, aren't changed.
= 

PTT time limit
= 

PTT from this program lets go by itself after this long
= 

DX CLUSTER
= 

Choose one
= 

Fill in from a list
= 

Server
= 

Commands after login
= 

Sent once logged in, with a ; between them. Each kind of cluster has its own: see the server's help. Usually empty.
= 

Keep spots for
= 

Show robot spots (Reverse Beacon Network)
= 

Spots from automatic CW and data skimmers. There can be a great many.
