BAND PLAN
= 

Country or region
= 

This program has a newer copy of this plan (%s). Reset uses it.
= 

Open plans folder
= 

Each plan is a JSON file you can edit. README.txt there explains the format.
= 

Reload
= 

Reads the files again, after you've edited one
= 

Reset this plan
= 

Can't write to %s
= 

Puts the built-in copy back. Your file is kept as .json.bak
= 

STATIONS
= 

Shown on the scope whichever band plan is chosen. See the Stations menu.
= 

%s (%d stations, revision %s). %s
= 

Open stations folder
= 

Each list is a JSON file you can edit, and you can add your own. README.txt there explains the format. Reload above reads them again.
= 

Reset station list
= 

Puts the built-in worldwide and broadcaster lists back. Your files are kept as .json.bak
= 

Puts the built-in worldwide, broadcaster and receiver lists back. Your files are kept as .json.bak
= 

Automatic (%s)
= 

Language
= 

Automatic follows the language this computer is set to. Choose one to keep to it whatever the computer uses. It changes straight away.
= 

Check GitHub for a new version at start
= 

Reads one small file from GitHub each time the program starts, and says on the bottom line if there's a newer build. Nothing about you or your radio is sent.
= 

Auto ON/OFF
= 

Switches the rig on when the program starts, and off when it closes. The rig's USB must stay powered for it to wake.
= 

Apply and reconnect
= 

Close
= 

Keys and rig set-up
= 

ON THE RIG  (MENU > SET > Connectors > CI-V)
= 

CI-V USB Port: Unlink from [REMOTE]
= 

CI-V USB Baud Rate: 115200
= 

CI-V USB Echo Back: OFF  (ON works too)
= 

CI-V Address: leave it at the default, 94h on an IC-7300 or A2h on an IC-9700
= 

USB AF Output Level (Connectors): raise it until the level bar sits below red
= 

USB SEND and USB Keying (Connectors > USB SEND/Keying): OFF
= 

KEYS
= 

Digits
= 

Start a frequency: 14.074, 14074, 7, 198k, +5. Enter goes there, Esc cancels.
= 

Left, Right
= 

Tune by the step. Hold Shift for ten times that.
= 

Up, Down
= 

Change the step
= 

Page Up, Page Down
= 

Next or previous band
= 

Find a station by name
= 

F1 to F8
= 

Data mode, next filter
= 

Split, swap VFOs
= 

PTT on or off, once armed
= 

Tuning dial
= 

Click and spin it. One turn is ten steps. Spin fast to move further; let go and it runs on.
= 

Wheel
= 

